5,1,1,talk,Daisuke,,Um... hello. I think we should look at what's actually happening on the floor. Maybe we could check the misrouted deliveries in the incident logs and the time lost to copying existing records?,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,May,,"Those sound like a good start, Daisuke! But we can't forget the people doing the work. I want to check the in-house developer availability and the staffing of the coordination group. We can't just assume everyone is free!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Practical points, as always. However, we're ignoring the external variables. I'll look into network coverage at customer plants and vendor licence pricing versus fixed-fee work. We can't let ""unforeseen"" site issues ruin the timeline again.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,"I agree with the need for practicality, but we must be cautious about the financial source. I will look into the capital budget and software allowance, as well as the outcomes of the last three internal rollouts.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Kenji,,"I think we're on the right track! To make sure we don't repeat old mistakes, I'll look into the outcomes of the last three internal rollouts and the record of cross-unit standardization efforts. Let's find something that lasts!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree with everyone. It's important to be careful. I just hope we don't overlook the small, daily struggles of the staff while focusing on the bigger budget and technical issues.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,May,,"Exactly, Daisuke! That's why I'm so focused on the staffing. It's easy to get dazzled by a fancy proposal, but if it breaks the people running it, it's a failure in my book. Right, everyone?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Shunichi,,"Emotional appeals are touching, May, but they don't fix a broken network or a budget shortfall. Let's keep our eyes on the actual constraints if we want a project that actually launches.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, you are correct about constraints. However, we must specifically identify which budget line is being used. If we miscalculate the source now, we will face a crisis during next year's renewal. We need a sustainable financial plan.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, I totally get that! But besides the money, I'm really curious about why some projects just disappear after a year. If we see a pattern in the rollouts, we can pick a winner that actually sticks!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... if we could, maybe we should also consider how vendor queries are handled? I'm worried that if the process is too complicated, the people on the floor will just give up on the new system.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, you're speaking my language! If the support system is a mess, the staff just ends up absorbing all that stress. We really need to be careful about who is actually doing the heavy lifting here.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Daisuke, @May, you're both obsessing over the ""feelings"" of the staff. While support is fine, it's irrelevant if the technical groundwork is a disaster. I'm sticking to the external risks; that's where the real failures happen.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, technical risks are significant, but financial instability is a certainty if we ignore the budget source. I believe we must prioritize the long-term cost structure over immediate operational preferences to ensure the project's survival.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, @Shunichi, you both make great points! But let's not forget that a project can be funded and technical, yet still fail because it doesn't fit our culture. I really want to see those past outcomes!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I understand. I'll stick with the misrouted deliveries and the time lost to copying records. I just want to make sure we help the people who are struggling with the small things every day.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,May,,I'm staying firm on my choices! I'll look into in-house developer availability and the staffing of the coordination group. Let's make sure we aren't just dreaming up projects that our exhausted staff can't actually support.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Shunichi,,I'll stick with network coverage at customer plants and vendor licence pricing. It's far more productive to identify the walls we're about to hit than to hope the staff feels better while the project stalls.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I will proceed with the capital budget and software allowance, and the outcomes of the last three internal rollouts. We must ensure the funding source is secure to avoid any surprises during next year's renewal.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Kenji,,"I'm all set! I'll look into the outcomes of the last three internal rollouts and the record of cross-unit standardization efforts. I can't wait to see what we find out! Let's do our best, everyone!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
