35,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... I found that we're losing nearly an hour every day just copying records that already exist. Also, there were eleven misrouted deliveries because different units have different addresses for the same firm. It seems like... small errors are causing real waste.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,May,,"That's exactly what I feared, Daisuke! My findings are even worse. Our developers are totally tied up until Q3, and the coordination group is a ghost town—two people are doing everything by hand. We're running on fumes!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It seems we're in for a disaster. Half the customer plants have dead zones in the afternoons, and getting device approval takes six weeks. If a proposal relies on real-time site access, it's dead on arrival.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The financial situation is precarious. The capital budget is frozen, meaning we can only afford projects funded by the recurring software allowance. Additionally, past rollouts show that broad, company-wide tools fail; only narrow, trade-specific tools survive.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, you're spot on! I found the same thing—projects that require everyone to enter data daily just disappear. Also, big standardization efforts usually fail unless they're for a specific area, like the tool room. We need something focused!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Ryuji, @Kenji... if broad tools fail, maybe we should focus on those specific, daily wastes I found? If we can fix the address errors and the copying, it would help the staff so much without needing a huge rollout.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, I'm with you, but only if it doesn't add more work to those two poor souls in coordination! If the ""fix"" just means more manual data entry, we're just moving the pain around.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, your concern for the ""poor souls"" is noted, but let's be rational. If we pick a project that requires constant site connectivity or per-head licensing, we're not just moving pain—we're inviting a total collapse. We need a narrow scope.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, I agree on the narrow scope. However, we must be strictly mindful that any project we choose must fit within the recurring software allowance. Since the capital budget is frozen, any proposal requiring upfront capital investment is impossible.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, @Shunichi, you're both right! If we want this to actually survive, we need a project that's narrow, fits the software budget, and doesn't force everyone to change their daily habits. Let's look for a ""small win""!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think a ""small win"" is exactly what we need. If we can just stop the misrouted deliveries and the copying, it would be a huge relief for the people on the floor. Does that sound... feasible?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, it sounds wonderful in theory, but ""feasible"" is the keyword. If the solution requires our missing developers or more manual logs from the coordination group, it's a fantasy. We need a win that doesn't cost us our sanity!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, sanity is a luxury; feasibility is a requirement. If the solution involves per-head licensing, the costs will spiral as we scale. We need a fixed-fee approach and zero reliance on customer-site networks. Anything else is just a gamble.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, I agree. A fixed-fee model is the only way to ensure we don't exceed the recurring software allowance. We must avoid any proposal that creates a hidden debt for next year's renewal.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, @Shunichi, I'm totally with you! Let's avoid those traps. If we find a proposal that's narrow in scope and doesn't need a huge team to maintain, it'll actually survive. I'm excited to see the candidates!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I hope the candidates have something that fits. I just want to make sure we don't pick something that sounds impressive but ignores the people who are actually struggling with these daily errors.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,May,,"Exactly! Let's be honest: we've all seen ""impressive"" projects that just end up as more work for the same exhausted people. If a candidate doesn't account for our staffing void, it's just a fancy way to burn out our team.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, your passion for the staff is admirable, but let's not let it cloud the logic. We need a project that is technically viable and financially stable. If it doesn't fit the constraints, it's useless.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, logic is exactly why I am concerned. We cannot afford to be optimistic. If a proposal relies on the frozen capital budget or creates recurring costs we cannot sustain, it is a failure before it begins. We must be rigorous.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I agree! Let's be rigorous but positive. If we find a project that's small, focused, and fits the budget, it'll be a huge win for everyone. I'm ready to see the candidates!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
